    "Notes Updated": "8/15/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "After falling down my list last year, he's moving right back up this year\n While the power numbers aren't showing up in home run's, he is impacting the ball with more authority than in the past\n He's been an above average hitter in the brutal hitting environment that is the Southern League\n Quick hands, ability to hit to all fields, still would like to see more elevation and more line drives especially\n Baserunning has taken a huge step forward, now a plus plus runner, he's more explosive and more refined as a basestealer than in the past\n Defense is elite. It's a 70 glove and a 60 arm\n There's a Sal Frelick type of outcome, as a switch hitter in there. Floor wise Blake Perkins feels pretty reasonable as an example.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "9/15/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Got off to a blazing start to his career in the DSL, but cooled down for a month or so, before finishing his first pro season pretty strong.\n Good speed, but struggled in stolen base attempts going only 7 for 14. A bit concerning.\n Good K BB%, kept strikeouts to a minimum.\n Bat to ball skills are good, though it seems like the swing decisions are what limited the K's.\n Could be a plus hitter, and shows some pop for a small guy. \n Off to a solid start in his pro career, hoping they push him to the ACL next year.",
